# Trivy ignore list for ghcr.io/penguintechinc/waddleai/ollama (hardened + debug).
#
# Two independent, unrelated categories of finding are ignored here. Do NOT
# blanket-carry this file forward on a version/base bump without re-running
# `trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL ghcr.io/penguintechinc/waddleai/ollama:hardened`
# (no --ignorefile) to see the live list first.
#
# SUPPRESSION POLICY (owner directive, 2026-09-08): a no-fix finding -- one
# where we are waiting on the vendor or upstream -- gets a TWO WEEK review-by
# date, not a multi-month one. Every entry below therefore carries
# "Review by <date>" no more than 14 days out, and the weekly re-triage
# workflow (.github/workflows/trivy-weekly-retriage.yml, via
# scripts/check-trivyignore-review-dates.sh) files an issue once that date
# passes. Short horizons are the point: these are bets that upstream will ship
# a fix, and a bet nobody revisits for three months is just a silent
# permanent exception. When re-triaging, re-verify the finding is still
# unfixed and push the date out another two weeks -- do not extend it further
# because it "keeps coming back".
#
# --- 1. Go module CVEs baked into the vendored upstream binary ---------------
# `gobinary`-class findings against usr/bin/ollama's embedded Go module build
# info (golang.org/x/*, stdlib, github.com/buger/jsonparser) — from
# ollama/ollama:0.32.13's own build, not introduced by this Dockerfile.
# Fixing these needs either a newer upstream release built with patched Go
# modules, or a from-source rebuild with a current Go toolchain — the latter
# is explicitly out of scope for spec §10.2 ("digest-pinned upstream base",
# not a from-source rebuild).
#
# Review by 2026-09-22. Retro-dated 2026-09-21 (audit-2026-09-14): these
# entries carried no review-by marker at all, so the weekly re-triage could
# never surface them and they had become permanent exceptions. Dated into
# the file's existing 2026-09-22 cohort rather than granted a fresh 14-day
# window -- they have never actually been re-verified, so they must not
# outlive the entries that have.
CVE-2026-25679
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136
CVE-2026-27137
CVE-2026-27145
