# --- 2. debian:trixie-slim baseline package CVEs, no fix published yet -------
# `debian`-class findings against packages already present in the *bare*
# debian:trixie-slim base (perl-base, util-linux, login, gzip, ncurses,
# libacl1, etc.) — every one carries Trivy status "affected" or
# "fix_deferred" with FixedVersion: None, meaning Debian security has not
# shipped a patched package yet; there is no version of this Dockerfile that
# can resolve them today.
#
# Confirmed NOT a trixie-specific regression: `trivy image debian:bookworm-slim`
# (the base every other image in this repo — proxy/Dockerfile,
# services/management/Dockerfile — is built on) carries the identical
# perl-base/util-linux/CVE-2026-53615 set as of the same scan date, so
# switching this image's runtime-base to trixie (required for glibc 2.39
# compat with ollama 0.32.13 — see the Dockerfile's top-of-file comment) did
# not introduce this exposure; it was already latent in the org's bookworm
# baseline and simply hadn't been scanned with an intact dpkg database
# before (see git history on this file — an earlier draft of the `hardened`
# stage deleted /var/lib/dpkg, which silently blinded Trivy's OS scanner
# into reporting a false "0 packages" clean result instead of actually being
# clean; that bug is fixed and this list reflects the real, dpkg-db-intact
# scan). Worth a follow-up ticket against proxy/management/webui's Trivy job
# (currently SARIF-only, non-blocking) to confirm whether they carry the same
# baseline set.
#
# Review by 2026-09-22. Retro-dated 2026-09-21 (audit-2026-09-14): these
# entries carried no review-by marker at all, so the weekly re-triage could
# never surface them and they had become permanent exceptions. Dated into
# the file's existing 2026-09-22 cohort rather than granted a fresh 14-day
# window -- they have never actually been re-verified, so they must not
# outlive the entries that have.
CVE-2026-53615
CVE-2026-41992
CVE-2026-54369
CVE-2025-69720
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-9538

# Added 2026-08-22 -- libssl3t64/openssl CVE-2026-14456 (OpenSSL QUIC server
# unbounded memory growth, HIGH). Trivy status "fix_deferred": Debian
# security has explicitly deferred shipping a patch -- Candidate == Installed
# (3.5.6-1~deb13u2) on both trixie/main and trixie-security as of this build,
# confirmed via `apt-cache policy libssl3t64 openssl` against this exact base
# digest, so no version of this Dockerfile can resolve it today. Contrast with
# the util-linux family (CVE-2026-53612/-53613/-53614), which surfaced in the
# same scan but DOES have a published fix on trixie-security -- those are
# pinned explicitly in the Dockerfile instead of ignored here. Review by
# 2026-09-22 or whenever `apt-cache policy libssl3t64` shows a newer
# candidate, whichever comes first.
CVE-2026-14456

# Added 2026-08-27 -- libsqlite3-0 CVE-2026-11822/-11824 (SQLite FTS5
# crafted-data arbitrary code execution + heap buffer overflow, both HIGH).
# Newly published/scored since the 08-22 refresh above (Trivy DB pulled
# 2026-08-27 for this scan, vs 08-22 when the rest of this file was
# calibrated) -- this is DB drift, not a regression introduced by any change
# to the Dockerfile. Trivy status "affected", FixedVersion: None for both
# (confirmed via `trivy image --format json`); `apt-cache policy
# libsqlite3-0` against this exact runtime-base shows Candidate == Installed
# (3.46.1-7+deb13u1) on both trixie/main and trixie-security, so Debian
# security has not shipped a patched package yet -- no version of this
# Dockerfile can resolve this today. Review by 2026-09-22 or whenever
# `apt-cache policy libsqlite3-0` shows a newer candidate, whichever comes
# first.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# --- 2026-09-07: util-linux CVE-2026-76642, no fix published ----------------
# Same DB-drift shape this file has hit before: the release build was green on
# 2026-08-29 (0d2eb51f) and red on 2026-09-08 (fef15bd1) with no Dockerfile or
# base-image change between them -- Trivy's vuln DB picked up a freshly
# published util-linux CVE. Hits the whole util-linux family shipped in the
# bare debian:trixie-slim base: bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1,
# libsmartcols1, libuuid1, mount, util-linux, util-linux-extra.
#
# Trivy status "affected" with an EMPTY FixedVersion column against installed
# 2.41.5-0+deb13u1 (see the build-ollama-image job log for run 34174626336) --
# Debian security has shipped no patched util-linux, so no rebuild and no
# version of this Dockerfile resolves it today. Not reachable from this image's
# workload either: nothing here invokes an external mount helper.
#
# Review by 2026-09-22, or whenever `apt-cache policy util-linux` against this
# runtime-base shows a Candidate newer than Installed, whichever comes first.
# The weekly re-triage workflow will flag it if a fix lands sooner.
CVE-2026-76642

# --- 2026-09-08: DB drift round two, after CVE-2026-76642 -------------------
# The 76642 entry above worked (it no longer appears in the gate output), but
# the vuln DB moved again between 09-07 and 09-08 and surfaced six more. Two
# distinct categories, verified separately rather than suppressed as a batch.
#
# (a) Debian base packages, no fix published. Trivy status "affected" with an
#     EMPTY FixedVersion against installed util-linux 2.41.5-0+deb13u1 and
#     systemd 257.13-1~deb13u1 -- same shape and same treatment as the rest of
#     category 2. Nothing in this image invokes an external mount helper,
#     nsenter, or systemd-homed, so none of these are reachable from its
#     workload.
#     Review by 2026-09-22. Retro-dated 2026-09-21 (audit-2026-09-14): this
#     sub-block was the only one of the 09-08 pair with no review-by marker,
#     so its four entries were invisible to the weekly re-triage. Dated into
#     the existing cohort, not given a fresh window.
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410
CVE-2026-16742
#
# (b) Go modules embedded in the vendored upstream binary -- category 1, but
#     these two report a FixedVersion, so they were checked before being
#     suppressed rather than assumed unfixable:
#       golang.org/x/crypto v0.43.0 (CVE-2026-56854, CRITICAL) -> fixed 0.55.0
#       golang.org/x/image  v0.22.0 (CVE-2026-46603, HIGH)     -> fixed 0.45.0
#     The fixed version is the MODULE's, not any consumable ollama release:
#     go.mod at v0.32.13 (pinned), v0.32.15 and v0.33.3 (latest stable, as of
#     2026-09-08) ALL still pin x/crypto v0.43.0 and x/image v0.22.0, so
#     bumping the base image fixes neither. Resolving them needs a from-source
#     rebuild with patched modules, explicitly out of scope for spec §10.2.
#     CVE-2026-56854 is in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh; this image serves HTTP and
#     exposes no SSH surface, so the package is linked but not reached.
#     ESCALATE AND RE-EVALUATE if an ollama release bumps x/crypto, or if the
#     deployment ever exposes an SSH listener. Review by 2026-09-22.
CVE-2026-56854
CVE-2026-46603
